winner_texts.kemeny_young:
The function \( f(x) = \frac{2x-7}{\sqrt{x^2-5x+6}} \) is defined only when the expression under the square root is positive (since we need real values and the denominator cannot be zero). The inequality \( x^2 - 5x + 6 > 0 \) factors as \( (x-2)(x-3) > 0 \). The quadratic opens upward and has roots at \( x = 2 \) and \( x = 3 \), so it is positive for \( x < 2 \) or \( x > 3 \). The numerator has no restrictions beyond being real.

Thus the domain is \( (-\infty, 2) \cup (3, \infty) \).

\boxed{(-\infty, 2) \cup (3, \infty)}

